comments:
I re-enabled this test since I had hard time repro the failure, even using roachprod stress.

Why do you thin we should not be closing the writer?  When I was debugging the above problem I definitely saw kvfeed seeing the expected error.  But, I think there might be a race in the changefeed_processor:
if errors.Is(err, kvevent.ErrBufferClosed) {
				// ErrBufferClosed is a signal that
				// our kvfeed has exited expectedly.
				err = nil
			}

What happens is we maybe blocked in the processor waiting for next message from buffer.Get.
We then get the schema change error, and we proceed to close blocking buffer.  Part of that action, will
wake up any waters (quota pool closed), then we immediately close(signalCh) -- which wakes up caller because it's waiting for signal channel in blocking buffer.get.  Then we try to pop another entry and return ErrBufferClosed -- which it is.
and I think we then check to see if error.Is(... ErrBufferClosed) -- and of course it is because (that's what we returned as a result of tick() function).  Then we proceed to check if the poller existed (changefeed_processors:453), but of we are racing between kvfeed returning and error and actually writing that error to the channel -- so we get nil.

At least that's what I think is happening.
